SCOPE (bead vms-0b6b / epic vms-da0, F1 of the GCC-as-VMS-oracle lane): this
bead needs GNU `as` (gas) plus the BFD/libiberty/opcodes it links — NOT gdb,
NOT ld, NOT gold, NOT the `binutils` driver-tools directory (ar/objcopy/
readelf/nm/strings/...), NOT gprof/gprofng. The upstream GNU FTP "binutils"
release tarball already excludes gdb/sim/gold's gdb-only pieces are absent by
construction; this vendoring additionally PRUNED, from the stock 2.43 release
tree, the following directories NOT needed to build gas: gold/, ld/, gprof/,
gprofng/, libctf/, elfcpp/, binutils/ (the ar/objcopy/readelf/nm/strings CLI
tools directory — distinct from this third-party/binutils/ vendor root; not a
build dependency of gas). Also pruned, everywhere they occur (bfd/, gas/,
opcodes/): testsuite/ (142M in gas/ alone — DejaGNU test fixtures, no build
role) and po/ (gettext translation catalogs) and doc/ (Texinfo manuals) —
none are inputs to compiling gas/bfd/opcodes/libiberty.

